=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "B", dense: true)[
  The knee allows movement in one plane only, like a door on hinges.
]

#sol-item(2, "A", dense: true)[
  A muscle can only pull, so a second muscle must pull the bone back the other way.
]

#sol-item(3, "B", dense: true)[
  Tendons join muscle to bone; ligaments join bone to bone.
]

#sol-item(4, "B", dense: true)[
  Water-filled cells pressing against their walls keep the tissue firm; lignified xylem supports woody plants.
]

#sol-item(5, "D", dense: true)[
  Bile is produced by the liver; the other three are genuine skeletal functions.
]

#sol-item(6, "A", dense: true)[
  A rounded head in a cup-shaped socket allows movement in every direction.
]

#sol-item(7, "B", dense: true)[
  Red marrow is the site of formation of red cells, white cells and platelets.
]

#sol-item(8, "C", dense: true)[
  The bones of the skull are interlocked and fused, allowing no movement.
]

#sol-item(9, "C", dense: true)[
  They pull in opposite directions, so they are antagonistic.
]

#sol-item(10, "D", dense: true)[
  Bone is largely calcium phosphate, and acts as a store for both elements.
]

#sol-item(11, "B", dense: true)[
  Without vitamin D (or calcium) the bones fail to harden and bend.
]

#sol-item(12, "D", dense: true)[
  Lignin in the xylem walls forms a rigid internal framework.
]

#sol-item(13, "C", dense: true)[
  Flat surfaces slide over one another, allowing limited movement.
]

#sol-item(14, "A", dense: true)[
  We decide when to move it, unlike smooth or cardiac muscle.
]

#sol-item(15, "A", dense: true)[
  The vertebrae enclose and protect the spinal cord, and support the head and trunk.
]

#sol-item(16, "B", dense: true)[
  The femur is the thigh bone, the longest bone in the body.
]

#sol-item(17, "C", dense: true)[
  Bone tissue is lost faster than it is replaced, so bones become fragile.
]

#sol-item(18, "A", dense: true)[
  Elasticity allows the joint to move without dislocating.
]

#sol-item(19, "D", dense: true)[
  The breastbone anchors the ribs at the front of the chest.
]

#sol-item(20, "D", dense: true)[
  Weight-bearing stress stimulates the bone-forming cells to lay down more bone.
]

#sol-item(21, "C", dense: true)[
  Turgor supports herbaceous plants; lignified xylem and sclerenchyma support woody ones.
]

#sol-item(22, "D", dense: true)[
  Smooth cartilage plus synovial fluid lubricates the joint.
]

#sol-item(23, "B", dense: true)[
  A sprain is the overstretching or tearing of a ligament at a joint.
]

#sol-item(24, "B", dense: true)[
  It forms the bowl that carries the weight of the upper body onto the legs.
]

#sol-item(25, "D", dense: true)[
  The femur is part of the appendicular skeleton (the limbs).
]

#sol-item(26, "C", dense: true)[
  To reverse a movement, a second muscle must pull the bone back.
]

#sol-item(27, "D", dense: true)[
  A peg rotating within a ring allows the head to turn from side to side.
]

#sol-item(28, "B", dense: true)[
  Bone matrix is largely calcium phosphate, giving it strength and rigidity.
]

#sol-item(29, "A", dense: true)[
  Both are needed for bone mineralisation, so their lack produces rickets in children.
]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true)[
  Wide, flattened roots at the base steady a tall trunk in shallow tropical soil.
]

